    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into June 5th with a primary objective of capitalizing on favorable matchups against Merrill Kelly and Brandon Young. **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the day\u2019s premier play (77.16), benefiting significantly from a premium batting order slot against Yesavage and a dynamic platoon advantage that pushes his efficiency rating into the high-70s. Joining him as a core engine for today\u2019s production, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.32) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.02) project as elite starts; **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces the vulnerable 4.75 xERA of Young, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** exploits a massive 14% platoon boost against Kelly. We are also monitoring **Nasim Nunez**, whose speed profile remains critical for our SB-starved roster; his score of 60.80 is bolstered by a 4% efficiency boost specifically derived from Kelly\u2019s slow delivery to the plate, making him a high-leverage start despite his projected spot at the bottom of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card involved the utility spot, where **Josh Jung** (45.33) narrowly missed the cut. While **Josh Jung** offers respectable pop, the optimizer favored the higher volatility and matchup upside of **Dominic Smith** (53.86) against Mitch Keller, as the latter\u2019s profile allowed for a more consistent path to counting stats. We are flagging the \"Lineup Pending\" status of **Nasim Nunez**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Curtis Mead**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, and **Gunnar Henderson** as a primary risk factor. Should these players slide down the order, their efficiency scores will suffer due to decreased RBI opportunities, particularly for **Curtis Mead** and **Jackson Merrill**. Managers should remain alert for late scratches, as our bench depth\u2014including **Miguel Vargas** and **Coby Mayo**\u2014is ready to plug any holes should the finalized cards shift our expected production curves.",
